# {{.Name}} — app runner

Thin runner for `packages/{{.Name}}`. The app code (a Go struct, without a
frontend) lives entirely in the package; this module only serves it.

| cmd               | mode                       |
| ----------------- | -------------------------- |
| `./cmd/{{.Name}}` | production and development |

## Port

- App (Go HTTP server): **{{.AppPort}}** — baked in the runner

## Run

```sh
make install    # once: this project's folders and dependencies
make dev        # air hot reload → http://localhost:{{.AppPort}}
```

## Production

```sh
cd ../..
go build -o ./apps/{{.Name}}/tmp/{{.Name}} ./apps/{{.Name}}/cmd/{{.Name}}
./apps/{{.Name}}/tmp/{{.Name}}   # → http://localhost:{{.AppPort}}, reads ./config.json
```

## Dev-mode notes

- `make dev` starts air from the repository root, so the runner reads and
  writes the root `config.json`.
- Air watches the `.go` files of `apps/{{.Name}}`, `packages/{{.Name}}` and the
  packages it imports (`config`, `store`), and rebuilds the runner on Go changes.
- The runner opens the database with `store.FromConfig()`, which creates it when
  it does not exist.
